<p>Hello world! This is my first blog post built with <strong>Jekyll</strong> and Markdown. Jekyll parses this text file and automatically compiles it into a static HTML page.</p>

<h2 id="formatting-options">Formatting Options</h2>

<p>You can easily format your text using normal Markdown syntax:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Bold text</strong> for emphasis</li>
  <li><em>Italics</em> for subtle highlights</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Inline code block</code> for code snippets</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="code-snippet-example">Code Snippet Example</h3>

<p>You can display styled code snippets using regular backticks or Liquid tags:</p>

<div class="language-javascript highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="c1">// Simple javascript alert</span>
<span class="nx">console</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">log</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="dl">"</span><span class="s2">Hello from Jekyll!</span><span class="dl">"</span><span class="p">);</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<h3 id="adding-images">Adding Images</h3>

<p>To add an image, reference your local assets folder:</p>

<p><img src="/assets/photos/self.jpg" alt="Blog Banner Image" title="Banner View" /></p>

